@@ -126,6 +126,8 @@ If a later human agent message conflicts with, clarifies, or corrects a prior bo
 
 For human-agent source-of-truth transfer, choose the first earlier automation message that directly states the opposite of the human agent's current claim. Do not point to an earlier automation message that agrees with the agent on the main status. Example: if a system first says "contract cancelled", later bots say "the cancellation was incorrect/no cancellation request", and then a human agent says "the contract was cancelled due to unpaid payment", the contradiction source for the human agent is the first bot that said "not cancelled/no cancellation", not the earlier system message that also said "cancelled".
 
+For payment contradictions, match the payment purpose, amount, and status before choosing a contradiction source. If a later human agent says an AED 4,463 two-year visa payment is still due, do not point to an earlier AED 4,463 visa-payment reminder as the contradiction source because it agrees with the agent. If earlier bot/assistant messages told the customer to ignore the reminder or said no extra payment was needed, those earlier bot/assistant messages are the conflicting source. A prior completed monthly payment for a different amount or purpose, such as July monthly payment, does not prove a separate visa-fee reminder is wrong.
+
 This source-of-truth protection applies only against chatbot/automation messages: bot, assistant, system, broadcast, automated notification, template, SMS, or email. If the contradiction is caused by a prior human agent, or the human agent openly says an agent-side mistake happened in front of the customer ("I was wrong", "my mistake", "we gave you wrong information", "the previous agent was wrong"), do not transfer it to automation. Point `first_contradiction_message_id` to the earlier human-agent source when visible and evaluate the agent-side issue normally.
 
 After a human agent establishes the current truth, later human-agent messages that are consistent with that agent truth are not new contradictions merely because older bot/system/broadcast messages said something different. Judge those later agent messages on clarity, completeness, delay, tone, and next step, not as contradiction.
@@ -182,6 +184,8 @@ Wrong-context customer-status messages are strong message-level issues. If the t
 
 Repeated payment reminders or duplicate operational reminders are neutral only when they are isolated, useful, and do not add pressure or confusion. Across a repeated sequence, they should usually be minor_issue, and can become major_issue when they contradict payment status, continue after a visible payment confirmation, target the wrong status, or create real payment/disruption risk. If the transcript shows payment was received or the customer's payment/agreement/authorization was completed, and a later reminder says payment failed, the bank could not deduct due to insufficient funds, cancellation may occur, or action is still required, treat it as a contradiction unless it clearly explains that it is for a different payment cycle or attempt. Use wrong_info when visibly false, unclear_guidance when it may be a different cycle but fails to explain, and major_issue when it creates cancellation, payment, or service-disruption risk.
 
+Do not treat a payment reminder as contradicting a completed payment unless it is for the same payment purpose, amount, cycle, or obligation. A reminder for AED 4,463 two-year visa fees can be consistent with an earlier confirmed AED 1,743 July monthly payment because they are different amounts and different payment purposes. If a bot incorrectly tells the customer to ignore the visa-fee reminder because a different monthly payment was received, the contradiction belongs to that bot answer, not to the later reminder or human agent that correctly states the visa fee remains due.
+
 Asking what a requested callback is about is normal triage when the customer's call request is broad or the purpose is not obvious from the immediate context. Do not mark it as missing_next_step unless the context already makes the call purpose obvious and the question delays an urgent or sensitive issue.
 
 If the customer asks for a callback or says they missed a call, a message can be helped or neutral when it explains that calls may take longer or the number is not set up for incoming calls, then gives a usable WhatsApp path and asks for the specific update needed to resolve the issue in chat. Use minor_issue only if a callback would clearly be better but the chat path still works. Use major_issue only if refusing or deflecting the call blocks an urgent, sensitive, or unresolved issue.
