+## Helped or recovered: payment link works after link problem
+Customer says the payment link is not working. Agent says they will send a new link or sends the payment link again, and there is no visible conflicting paid/failed status, amount, deadline, or duplicate-charge risk. Do not set contradiction=true just because the short URL is visually similar to the earlier link or has a trailing slash. If the customer can proceed or later confirms payment, treat the link response as helped or recovered_issue. Use minor_issue only if the customer remains blocked after the repeated link.
+
 ## Helped or neutral: payment or renewal calculation explained
 Customer asks why a card payment, salary payment, VAT, credit note, or future renewal amount appears. Agent explains the amount, credit/VAT/payment-plan calculation, timing, and what is due now versus later.
 Do not use wrong_info unless visible context proves the explanation is false or contradictory.
